{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And Moses said to Hobab</b> – I have already explained in (Exodus 2:16) that Hobab is a new name given to Jethro when he returned to the faith of Israel, for this is the way of every convert — a different name is given to His servants. Now Moses entreated him to go with them, saying to him simply, \"and we will treat you well,\" and he [Hobab] supposed that they would give him from the spoil silver and gold and garments and flocks and cattle, but he would have no inheritance among them. Therefore he was unwilling and answered, \"No, to my land and to my kindred I will go,\" for there I have inheritance and possessions and honor. Then Moses said to him, \"Please do not leave us,\" for with your knowledge the wilderness will be our eyes in the conquest of the lands, and you will guide us on the route by which we shall go up, and from all that good which HaShem will do for us we will do good to you — he hinted at giving him a holding in a good land as his wage for his trouble and the help he would provide them in the conquest of the land. In my opinion he was satisfied with this and did so, as I mentioned there (Exodus 18:1). And thus they said in the Jerusalem Talmud (Bikkurim 1:4): The descendants of the Kenite, the father-in-law of Moses, bring first fruits and recite the declaration, as it is written: \"Come with us and we will treat you well.\""], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:04:04.232082732Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}